/* _plsw_storage.msw -- PL/SW heap allocator runtime
 *
 * Provides _PLSW_GETMAIN / _PLSW_FREEMAIN procedures backed by
 * a free-list allocator over a statically-declared heap region.
 * The PL/X-style ?GETMAIN / ?FREEMAIN macros are not implemented
 * in v1; PL/SW's MACRODEF/GEN system emits assembly only and
 * can't synthesize the right code for arbitrary expression-typed
 * LENGTH or arbitrary lvalue-typed ADDRESS arguments. Future
 * saga: add macros once PL/SW's macro system supports AST-level
 * expansion. Until then, call the procedures directly.
 *
 *   %INCLUDE _plsw_storage;       -- entry module: impl + heap
 *
 *   %DEFINE PLSW_STORAGE_HEADERS_ONLY 1;
 *   %INCLUDE _plsw_storage;       -- non-entry module: header only
 *
 *   %DEFINE PLSW_HEAP_SIZE 32768; -- override default 64KB heap
 *   %INCLUDE _plsw_storage;
 *
 * Calling convention (call as ordinary PL/SW procedures):
 *   P  = _PLSW_GETMAIN(N);            P=0 on OOM
 *   RC = _PLSW_FREEMAIN(P, N);        RC=0 on success,
 *                                     1=double-free/invalid,
 *                                     2=size mismatch
 *
 * See docs/storage-allocation.md for the full design.
